    "body": "@matt-h This seems like a plausible feature to add! And it doesn't seem that hard to do either.\r\n\r\nIf we refactor all of the modules to be consistent so that the version segment is called `version`, then we can check for a config value, let's say `version`, and if that is false we don't show that segment. The default of the config value would be true though.\r\n\r\nNow that I think of this, this is a great way to declutter your prompt. I might use this when it's implemented!",
