    "created_at": "2019-09-30T18:46:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-30T18:46:49Z",
    "body": "@bijancn I can imagine a use case where you just want to know what's in a project without manually parsing all the possible filetypes. For example, if I pop into a new project, there might be a CMake file, a few python scripts, and package file, but not any nodejs (random example, let's just roll with it).\r\n\r\nI can imagine being more interested in knowing that those conditions/files exist than in exactly what versions they all are. The way to do this without a prompt to help you would be to run `ls -a` and then do a manual parse on all the files you see.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
